{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465949-world-building-how-do-you-use-certain-clans","id":1465949,"title":"[World-Building] How do you use certain clans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-30T17:11:42-07:00","id":1465949,"title":"[World-Building] How do you use certain clans?","content":"A spin-off from the Sabbat: The Blackhand thread where we got into discussing the role of the Ventrue in the Camarilla as well as Toreador. This is a thread for how you like to roleplay various Clans and how good they are at their assigned roles.<br /> <br /> Basically, no wrong answers here but a way of talking about how you see them filling various roles in Cainite society.<br /> <br /> Ups and downs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T17:25:32-07:00","id":1465952,"title":"","content":"Stereotypes are stereotypes, but the clans have been around for thousands and thousands of years and different clans have gotten a reputation for different things. And in general, the reputation is more accurate than not. The Nosferatu as a whole tend to be pretty good spies. The Ventrue has a whole tend to be decent leaders. The Malkavians can often bring insights that other clans can't.<br /> <br /> Of course you can absolutely have Ventrue who are complete fuckups at leadership roles, or Nosferatu who couldn't sneak their way through an empty room. But for the most part, more often than not, a member of a clan will be at least somewhat decent at the thing the clan is known for. Not necessarily the best, not necessarily better than members of other clans at the thing, but at least a bit above average.<br /> <br /> So if you need help breaking into a building, you'd ask a Nos for assistance. If you need help in manipulating a group of mortals you'd turn towards a Toreador. And even if the one vampire you turn towards couldn't help you, they very likely know someone in their clan who could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T17:27:45-07:00","id":1465953,"title":"","content":"<b>How do I roleplay the Clans 1#: Ventrue?</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Ventrue</b><br /> <br /> Generally, the Ventrue of the Camarilla are people that struggle with the fact that they're viewed as a necessary evil in Kindred society. They're mostly embraced from the privileged elites of society and are used to everything going their way. Furthermore, their powers are tailor made for assembling a power base of wealth as well as influence. There is almost never a poor Ventrue unless they are a fantastic moron or the subject of enemy action. However, the Ventrue struggle to deal with the fact that they are the leaders by default rather than acclaim.<br /> <br /> In the simplest terms, the Ventrue can't compel the majority of vampires to obey them very well. The Brujah are resistant to any form of orders, the Nosferatu have their own hierarchy, the Gangrel don't CARE about leadership, the Toreador are the real masters of the game, the Tremere have their own hierarchy x11 (and don't respect anyone who can't pull a rabbit out of a hat), and the Malkavians? Well, there you go. The power of the Ventrue means they can compel <i>mortals</i> to obey them through force or majesty but Kindred are much more resistant. So Ventrue inevitably end up using money, violence, and tradition to try to assert their specialness over all other Clans.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue believe themselves to be the natural rulers of vampiredom and heirs to Caine but this is not an attitude that the rest of Cainite society takes all that seriously. Generally, the best they can get is, &quot;Ventrue rule is the worst form of government except for all the others.&quot; Someone has to bribe the mortal photographers and erase memories after all. For a Clan culture and blood that <i>demands</i> respect and obedience, a huge number of Ventrue quietly seethe at the fact other vampires don't automatically defer to them in all things. A few Ventrue decide they must thus PROVE themselves to be the best possible leaders while others lash out in petty displays of vulgar excess or tyranny to vent their frustration.<br /> <br /> Vampire society couldn't function without the Ventrue doing the grunt work of protecting the Masquerade and accumulating mortal influence but its hard to be an aristocracy when the peasants can punch through walls and ALSO compel you to love them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T17:42:53-07:00","id":1465957,"title":"","content":"<b>How do I roleplay the Clans 2#: Toreador</b><br /> <br /> If you can read someone's mind <i>and</i> control someone's emotions then there is absolutely nothing preventing you from making them dangle on a puppet string. The Ventrue can compel you to do whatever they want and make you believe they are the best person for the job. The Toreador have you think it was your own idea and they're a bunch of harmless socialites. The Toreador are the true masters of the Camarilla and it exists in a very real way because of their efforts. Not because they want to protect the Masquerade, though that is obviously there, but because the Toreador wanted to create a vampire society that they could be the mean girls and popular boys of. Elysium, the politicing, the status, and intrigue? All of the inherent backstabbing and social climbing inherent to the Camarilla is the product of Toreador maneuvering. So much so that no one usualy questions why it even exists.<br /> <br /> Why were the Brujah kicked out? Because the Toreador decided that they were no longer any fun and constantly ruining their fun. Why is the Camarilla now a much more exclusive old boys (and girls) club? Because the Toreador got stick of the tenor of the place being lowered. Thin Bloods and Caitiff can trace massive amounts of their persecution to the Degenerates' utterly pointless classicism designed to make an in-group versus an out group.<br /> <br /> The Toreador are the grandmasters of social combat and their best argument for being even better at it than the Ventrue is the fact that they are routinely dismissed as compared to the Tremere or Ventrue as the beating heart of the Camarilla. Even Anarchs think they're a bunch of fashionistas and snobs rather than propagandists or schemers. Their pretensions of artistry and patrons of beauty fall before the fact they are much-much better at stirring up shit. It's entirely possible THEY created the Ventrue's superiority/inferiority complex.<br /> <br /> They need to feel alive because so much of their power is about making fake emotions and knowing how to manipulate people.<br /> <br /> Ironically, the Toreador's greatest weakness is the fact that <i>they can't turn this off</i>. Being able to know the true emotions and thoughts of everyone they know with Auspex means that virtually every Toreador eventually becomes the heartless manipulative sociopath vampires are always accused of being. They can't stop backstabbing, one-upping, undermining, and playing the Game even when they want to have genuine alliances. Its an addiction and a source of major instability in every Camarilla society.<br /> <br /> No domain can be stable if Annabelle's shoes were maroon at a red-shoe party. If they can't find drama, they will make it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-30-2021, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T18:15:14-07:00","id":1465963,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's quite accurate about the Toreador, simply because I tend to think that Clan Compulsions are at work subconsciously even when they aren't outright active the way a Bestial makes them. Which means that most Toreador really do want to create art and be surrounded by beauty. Consequently they are going to have hobbies that take up a decent chunk of their time.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Ventrue Clan Compulsion working on a subconscious level means that most of them are trying to accumulate social power literally from the moment they wake up until the moment they fall asleep, and they may even be dreaming up social climbing schemes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 10-30-2021, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T18:21:50-07:00","id":1465964,"title":"","content":"I accept the existence of the clan stereotypes by viewing them as cultures that have been passed down from sire to impressionable new childe for generations.<br /> <br /> The one clan that I really relish tweaking, though, is the Nosferatu. They may have put in a lot of work in recent decades to market themselves as information brokers in order to carve out a space for themselves in the prestation economy, but their real culture as a clan is one of doomsday preppers.<br /> <br /> There's a passage about the Guruhi in the Ebony Kingdom book, about a peacefully negotiated end to hostilities within the clan, that certainly lends itself to a reading in which the Nictuku gave up hunting the rest of Absimiliard's children *centuries ago.*<br /> <br /> This is too funny for me to not hold it dear as cherished headcanon. It keeps me warm on cold nights. A storyline that was otherwise never going to be resolved is tied up in a neat bow. One of the biggest secrets in the European and American World of Darkness is completely unguessed at by the great sewer detectives, *and it's about their own clan.* Every time the Sewer Rats lose communication with their kin in another city, it's probably another supernatural competitor for the same turf - Black Spiral Dancers or Bone Gnawers, Sluagh or Redcaps, the Tzimisce under Manhattan - the great detectives never get to the bottom of it because they assign blame to a menace that only exists in their heads.<br /> <br /> If Baba Yaga's really dead, the werewolves did it, but you'll never convince the paranoid Nosferatu of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T19:21:15-07:00","id":1465966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465949-world-building-how-do-you-use-certain-clans?p=1465963#post1465963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's quite accurate about the Toreador, simply because I tend to think that Clan Compulsions are at work subconsciously even when they aren't outright active the way a Bestial makes them. Which means that most Toreador really do want to create art and be surrounded by beauty. Consequently they are going to have hobbies that take up a decent chunk of their time.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Ventrue Clan Compulsion working on a subconscious level means that most of them are trying to accumulate social power literally from the moment they wake up until the moment they fall asleep, and they may even be dreaming up social climbing schemes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'm not saying the Toreador don't love beauty and artistry but it's also something they define by constantly pushing their status and prestige over others. Beauty in nature is inherently comeptitive.<br /> <br /> Peacocks strutting around are some of the most violent and dangerous birds around.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T23:53:02-07:00","id":1465975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465949-world-building-how-do-you-use-certain-clans?p=1465952#post1465952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stereotypes are stereotypes, but the clans have been around for thousands and thousands of years and different clans have gotten a reputation for different things. And in general, the reputation is more accurate than not. The Nosferatu as a whole tend to be pretty good spies. The Ventrue has a whole tend to be decent leaders. The Malkavians can often bring insights that other clans can't.<br /> <br /> Of course you can absolutely have Ventrue who are complete fuckups at leadership roles, or Nosferatu who couldn't sneak their way through an empty room. But for the most part, more often than not, a member of a clan will be at least somewhat decent at the thing the clan is known for. Not necessarily the best, not necessarily better than members of other clans at the thing, but at least a bit above average.<br /> <br /> So if you need help breaking into a building, you'd ask a Nos for assistance. If you need help in manipulating a group of mortals you'd turn towards a Toreador. And even if the one vampire you turn towards couldn't help you, they very likely know someone in their clan who could.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a very fair way to do it. Not every vampire is a stereotype but these stereotypes are created by certain vampires acting that way and Embracing people like themselves.<br /> <br /> Like, there may not actually be THAT many Ventrue tyrants but the thing is Lodin and Queen Anne Bowesley are both Ventrue tyrants and their reputation IS the Ventrue Prince reputation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T00:11:21-07:00","id":1465977,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan Thoughts #3: Tremere</b><br /> <br /> I tend to view the Tremere as individuals who are almost comically enslaved to their own reputations.<br /> <br /> This could be way off but my general view about the Tremere, especially Pre-V5 but still after, is the fact that they stuck playing the role of the power-hungry evil sorcerers. The average Tremere is Embraced from a University grad student rather than people at the end of their lives and would probably spend the next century of their life researching without much complaint. Letf to their own devices, the Tremere are some of the most <i>boring</i> individuals you might ever meet in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> However, the nature of the Tremere is the fact that they are constantly required to justify their existence in the Camarilla even centuries later. The Tremere are constantly trotted out for every single problem imaginable ranging from, &quot;Who murdered Dave?&quot;, &quot;What is Steve's Clan? Is he really Ventrue?&quot;, &quot;Is this house really haunted?&quot; The Tremere also stereotyped as being ambitious power-hungry psychopaths so they are always the first people that a would-be usurper is approached whenever there's a coup planned. Many Tremere actually resent the titles of Seneschal and Primogen that are forced onto them as &quot;rewards&quot; for being there to do their wizardry. The Tremere play the games of prestation like all Kindred but have an embarrassment of riches they often have little use for.<br /> <br /> Tremere do not <i>care</i> whether the other Clans respect them. They only care if the other Clans get in their way. Many Tremere Regents think of themselves as the janitors of their city, cleaning up after incompetent Princes and Harpies because the only way they can do their research in peace is in a stable non-Sabbat, non-Hunter filled cities. This means preserving the Masquerade, managing business interests to keep themselves funded, and trying to avoid all-out wars they will be caught up in. Power to the Tremere is the raw magic of their Disciplines and mortal or even Kindred power will almost always be a dull substitute.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You don't understand power, Grand Admiral Thrawn. Conquering worlds you'll never even visit isn't power. Neither is destroying ships and people and rebellions you haven't looked at face-to-face.&quot; </i>\u2015Joruus C'baoth<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Power is power,&quot; </i>-- Cersei Lannister<br /> <br /> Which is ironic because there is a place that the Tremere toss aside all of their traditional apathy to Kindred politics and boredom to become Toreador gerbils on coffee. Tremere <i>hate</i> other blood mages, particularly other Tremere. There is seething resentment and ambition hiding behind the eyes of virtually every Apprentice that bringing another Warlock into your home is taking your life into your own hands.<br /> <br /> It's ironic for a Clan that used to be ritually blood bonded to itself but every Tremere plots against each other. They jockey for power, prestige, and access to the forbidden tomes. They undermine each other, sabotage one another, seduce, and even plot murders when they're not readying for duels to the final death. All of it for the glory of the Clan, of course, and the fact House Carna and House Tremere are feuding doesn't mean they won't team up against outsiders. In the end, other vampires aren't really &quot;real.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Tremere hate the Banu Haqim less because of the fact the latter have tried to kill them for millennia and more because the later have Blood Sorcery. The same for the Tzimisce. A Caitiff who knows Blood Sorcery is targeted because he's a valid target in the game but the intensity of the hatred is not that different from their own in-clan rivals. A secret is only valuable the fewer people who know it after all and a Tremere measures themselves against other magicians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T00:28:19-07:00","id":1465981,"title":"","content":"I think that I run the Clans pretty close-to-book. My chronicles are V20, with frequent bits of &quot;deep lore&quot; taken from the Revised-era Clanbooks, and bits and pieces taken from V5's additions to the Metaplot. Having run VTM now for a little over two years, trends have certainly emerged in the way I tend to play NPCs of certain clans, emphasizing certain aspects.<br /> <br /> <b>Brujah</b> tend to be intense and passionate, but often surprisingly well-controlled. Brujah who make it to Ancilla status tend to be ones with Self Control of 4 or better. They aren't always dedicated to a higher cause or philosophy but they do tend to be social, joining groups and accumulating followers. You rarely see a Brujah on their own, they almost always have gangmates and mortal followers (cultivated via <i>Presence</i> rather than <i>Dominate</i>, these Allies and Herd tend to be quite outspoken and willful). They are one of the most common clans by number, especially in the lower age range.<br /> <br /> <b>Toreador</b> are flashy, scintillating, bitchy and have a definite tendency to be some of my cruelest characters. They often dress outrageously, costumed to attract attention. Their culture strongly emphasizes the art of the put-down. Many of them are purely social creatures who rely on the rules of the Camarilla to protect them, but the occasional &quot;wareador&quot; will be among the deadliest Kindred in my settings. They are also an extremely common Clan, filing up Kindred gatherings and dominating any social scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Malkavians</b> come in two varieties. I haven't much used standard Malkavians, with the Dominate variety being much more common in my <b>Northwest by Night</b> chronicle due to the city's Malkavian Primogen having a very large brood. Dominate Malkavians tend to function much like the stereotypical Ventrue, building power structures around themselves (in the Primogen's case, a powerful regional crime syndicate). There's a little bit of envy there---the Malkavians see how power, influence and respect comes so <i>easily</i> tlo the Ventrue, and they are weighed down by their derangements and negative stereotypes among the Kindred. Their derangements are rarely as obvious as the <i>Dementation</i>-using side of the Clan and tend towards deformation of personality---rage, paranoia, envy magnified to maniacal proportions. As a result the clan tends to stand apart and operate much like a family--often squabbling and fractious, but ready to support one another against the Kindred who fear and despise then.<br /> <br /> Most of the <b>Assamite</b> NPCs I've used are of the Vizier variety and I emphasize the Clan's learned, cultured aspects. Poetry, history, philosophy and faith are deeply woven into their clan culture. Playing the Assamite Primogen is exhausting because I work hard to weave poetry from Rumi or Omar Khayyam into much of her dialogue, which requires reading and preparation beforehand.<br /> <br /> With <b>Ventrue,</b> (as you might guess, one of my favorite Clans) I emphasize the collegial aspect of their clan's culture. They act as one, almost always presenting a united front when dealing with other clans in the city. This compensates for the fact that they are one of the fewest clans by number--only the worthy[ will be selected for embrace, and pass through the long trials of the <i>agogwe</i>. Necessarily they are few in number, but their vast resources, competence and cooperative culture more than makes up for this. Beneath that front however, their ambition drives them to dark deeds and endless plotting. I dig the corporate aspect of the modern clan and they mainly subside in the worlds of high finance, technology or business and politics, with a few outliers rooted in the city's underworld. They are snobbish and competitive but also brokers and deal-makers. Their pride is both a source of strength---they are in some ways the most &quot;selfless&quot; clan--and their downfall.<br /> <br /> <b>Gangrel</b> are mysterious. They come and go through the borders of the city at will, prowling where other Kindred fear to tread and inhabiting the desolate and liminal areas of the city. Other Kindred know to give their claws a wide berth. They always seem to be outsiders and loners, for few can guess how deeply bound together the Gangrel are by their oral legends and traditions. Getting to know a Gangrel NPC over an extended period will show how deeply bound these &quot;loners&quot; are by obligations to their Clan. The few who try to join the Camarilla tend to be treated rather badly, used as fodder and scarcely allowed to gain status by Kindred who misunderstand and quietly fear them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","user":"Ventrue Busboy","date":". 10-31-2021, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T00:46:03-07:00","id":1465984,"title":"","content":"To me the Gangrel seem to be the most in tune with being vampires, and are therefore the most baffled by clans that care about things that have nothing to do with vampire existence. When your flesh is cold and hard, there is no meaningful difference between a bed with silk sheets and an air-conditioner, and literally sleeping in the dirt. When you feed on blood, there is no meaningful difference between being able to afford caviar and only being able to afford 99 cents a pack hotdogs. You can't eat either of them.<br /> <br /> They avoid the other clans because the other clans are constantly trying to pull them into conflicts over pointlessly human things like wealth, or who controls the art museum.<br /> <br /> Life for a vampire is incredibly simple: enjoy hunting and feasting on blood, sleep wherever is safe because your undead body has no need for &quot;comfort&quot;, preserve the masquerade because it allows you to hunt in peace. Everything else is just the other clans being too stupid to notice that they are not human anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T02:29:13-07:00","id":1465991,"title":"","content":"Clans are natural self-fulfilling stereotypes. <br /> <br /> IMO most common Disciplines are learnt via hunting behaviours. Presence is usually gained by charming your fangs into someone, Potence is gained by holding them down and so on and so forth. Or if you want to say the chicken comes first, Someone good with Dominate will have an easier time manipulating someone into being fed from, and anyone is going to use the methods easiest for them. In any case, Someone with a lot of levels in Potence will be more likely to use physical force to feed, and can't be described as a gentle person. Disciplines offer a Positive feedback loop: Once one strategy for feeding becomes easy, the more you can rely on it. The more you use it, the easier it gets. <br /> <br /> You add in the weaknesses and boom, it becomes very easy to become the archetype. The clan culture follows. Most clans have a culture that very naturally follows their disciplines and weakness. They in turn become very likely to embrace good fits. Deviance isn't impossible, but you're likely to become a Caitiff as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T02:49:52-07:00","id":1465992,"title":"","content":"Toreador, and perhaps some of you may find this ironic, are barely a clan, and are somewhat resented for it. The largely benign weakness and Generalist disciplines allow nearly anyone to ve a Toreador. They don't have much direction like the other big clans. They are the least unified and infight more than any other clan, though they are unified (and populous) enough that they aren't to be easily trifled with. As individuals they are often incredibly successful. The best and worst can be counted among their number. <br /> <br /> Conversely, Malks are also very diverse in who they are and what they do. Malkavians can ordinarily be found in the company of other clans. They dance with the Toreador, conduct business with the ventrue, discuss lore with the Tremere or secrets with the Nosferatu and run amok with the Brujah. However, weakness trully binds them together, and despite the disparaty of their members they can come together when the time calls for it. Their different perspectives and expertises gives them an overwhelming advantage in information and resource diversification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T09:50:48-07:00","id":1466023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465949-world-building-how-do-you-use-certain-clans?p=1465964#post1465964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Baba Yaga's really dead, the werewolves did it, but you'll never convince the paranoid Nosferatu of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree and run like that in my games, but unfortunately there is official lore in the matter.<br /> <br /> It doesn't preclude the Niktuku being now at peace with the rest of the clan, by the way, but at least Baba Yaga was officially offed by one. She was a big jerk and their sister, anyway, so it may be a more personal matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> My take on stereotypes is that I don't like 'em, period. For several reasons that apply in several ways.<br /> <br /> But the main reason is that Kindred embrace Humans, and those humans had their own personal history and personality before anyways. You can't play this as secondary as by definition you lost the formative years of that person. You can decide that trauma + supernatural + whatever overrides it as the main source of personality and behavior, but I find this approach as unlikely as boring, so to Hell with stereotypes.<br /> <br /> What can be said of the clans, though, is that they still have a culture. Not as pervasive as an ethnic culture, but culture is a complex construct that exists in many layers. Your gaming group have an internal culture. So yes, clans have a culture that interacts and permeates other cultural constructs that inform individual behavior.<br /> <br /> Embrace expectations also play a big role. What kind of people are likely to be Embraced into a given clan. There are some trends because it isn't just a matter of personal taste, as you're pressed by your peers into some choices and may not have permission if not following through. Disciplines and Weakness certainly play a role, but a minor one. Clan structure plays a greater role on how the clan behaves as a whole, but is also secondary to individual personality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T11:08:14-07:00","id":1466034,"title":"","content":"<b>Ventrue</b><br /> <br /> <i>Embrace:</i> The Ventrue look for people that can carry out clan ambitions. They look for competence and drive, and they are more likely than most to interfere on an individual member's choice of Childe, so not following their style is a dangerous prospect. That way we can expect that most of them were at least good prospects in life, at least as far as it could be guessed.<br /> <br /> It doesn't means every Ventrue was rich or successful in life, or that just being rich places you in their radar. Life is a bitch and the real world isn't as meritocratic as some people think, if it will ever be, and most Ventrue know it, so sometimes a jewel can be find among the downtrodden, and a great number of the upper echelons of mortal society can't really make it as Ventrue.<br /> <br /> But the trend is still there, of course. It <i>is</i> easier to develop and show your talent when life already blessed you, while poverty may kill it too soon. The new rich tend to be higher profile in general society than members of rich traditional families, which make them a bit hard to remove and Embrace. And of course, knowing exceptions exist don't eliminate bias completely. In the end, the majority of the Ventrue was &quot;well born&quot; in life and is used to be on the top of the ladder.<br /> <br /> <i>Structure:</i> probably the second most structured clan in the Camarilla, the Ventrue are accompanied by their peers from afar from Embrace to Final Death. They are selected, prepared, trained and indoctrinated. It isn't too much of a thorough indoctrination, though, more geared towards efficient service than anything, but is still intense. After that they're still watching, offering help and demands for every member.<br /> <br /> That makes little for informing behavior directly, but weeds out most of the problematic newcomers and continually creates prestation within the clan. A Ventrue Vampire isn't a stereotype, but exists in continual service to the Ventrue Institution, with varying levels of actual belief in, agreement with or compliance to this institution.<br /> <br /> <i>Weakness:</i> certainly the clan Weakness creates a pressure no Ventrue can ignore. On one hand, the variety of it means they'll have to develop far different strategies to form and keep their herds and feeding grounds. On the other though, all of them must develop the skills to put those strategies to work, so all of them must be pragmatic and organized, with a good long term vision and people skills.<br /> <br /> Or, at least, be able to delegate this to someone competent. Delegation is an important ability in itself, so yeah, that work, too.<br /> <br /> <i>Disciplines:</i> it's easy to attribute success to the combination of Dominate and Presence, and in a certain way this is true, but here is the thing: those are hard to use Disciplines. Not hard on their use, but hard on their long term outcomes. Few powers are so likely to backfire royally on the user if applied without care. Dominated people are pliable but relatively obvious, and it only gets worse if they're Dominated with frequency. Presence creates drive, but little direct control over the targets' actions.<br /> <br /> Given the Ventrue's necessities and ambitions, they are more powerful for what they must learn to use their powers sparingly than by just using them. They learn what makes people tick, without the benefit of just see it. They learn how to select targets and influence without pressure. They can completely overcome someone's will, true. But what a single person means to them? If you brainwash a police captain all you get is an early retired police captain. Controlling the police department takes a lot more of cunning.<br /> <br /> Fortitude helps with the two other things they will need, survival and lots of patience. As masters behind so many people, even without imposing their will, the Ventrue are the obvious targets. As the people that will be present at high profile meetings, they're on the hot-spots of violence. As the charismatic generals in battles literal and metaphorical, they are the ones to take the shot. As leaders that must keep morale, they must take the shot and shrug it off. And as master planners trying to reach beyond their direct powers, they must be used to spend most of their time just waiting.<br /> <br /> <i>Culture:</i> the clan is deeply informed by the upper classes and by high administration. Once it meant the Senatus, then it meant the military, now it means big investors. One way or another, everyone watches everyone else's achievements and have to meet expectations.<br /> <br /> A big difference from the Ventrue to some aristocratic groups is their take on personal value, though. Your value is defined by your work to the clan. Your pedigree may play a role, but ultimately they are perfectly willing to throw a prince under the bus if they do little for the greater whole, and protect a peasant with true ability to achieve.<br /> <br /> In the end no matter how you define aristocracy, the clan remember the time when it meant nothing and knows the tides will change anew. And this is something to be taught at the <i>agogwe</i>, so it doesn't matter how much you believe your blood, live and dead, matters, you know it won't save you if you mess up.<br /> <br /> Work to the greatness of the clan. Keep the stability of Kindred society. Organize people, this is more important than ruling them. Let fools be fools, but make them reach the goals. Stay focused. Be a part of the whole and reap the benefits we can achieve together.<br /> <br /> <i>Characters:</i> Many Ventrue came from structured backgrounds and went through a structured learning process after an embrace into a structured clan. They may have wildly different views of the entire thing, but they're well adapted to work within it.<br /> <br /> It is easy then to miss their actual variety. Those people are very used to presenting an unified front even when it is far from it or unnecessary. Most of them are also used to hierarchy, and to act from near the top of it, especially if they were rich in life, so acting accordingly is like second nature to them. It doesn't mean they're necessarily tyrants, or even that they're as arrogant as they seem, but they likely seem the part for people unused to this sort of ambient.<br /> <br /> That way, Ventrue tend to follow through with the system despite their actual opinions about it. Some willingly choose to remain in lesser positions because it fits their personal preferences for one reason or another. Some game the system for personal gain, other do so to help the downtrodden, but go unseen for not speaking overtly against it. They are just used to the idea that bashing it doesn't work. Some will try to build their own power base to act against it, which obviously mean that even when they act against the clan, they look like the clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T19:00:06-07:00","id":1466080,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I think clans are something that is too often emphasized in games. Obviously clans provide a lot of the culture of the vampire, and some clans have more rigid structures than others. But I've seen too many games where the politics of a domain are driven almost entirely by clans as if they were some group that commanded absolute loyalty by its members, and I don't see that. That was a real problem in some of the LARPs I've been in, and I always disliked it because I felt it tended to hijack the game rather than contribute to it.<br /> <br /> I think they are best seen as large, extended families. You have some obligation to others of your blood, and you see each other during family gatherings, but otherwise that's it. Actual politics are much more personal. You can have rivals and enemies inside your clan just as easily as those outside of it. In so far there is any true loyalty of those of the same clan, it's more likely to between broodmates and sire-childer - the immediate family of a far larger extended family with various prominent lineages and distant branches often being separate families. The smaller the group, the more likely they have common interests.<br /> <br /> Even for the more centralized clans, that structure is there for vampires who want to raise their status or influence within the clan. No vampire must to do that. You can be the black sheep of the clan and don't have anything to do with that. Or be the person who shows up, but contributes nothing. Even for a clan like the Tremere, which is the example of centralized internal control, we had the immediate examples of Garwood Marshall who didn't contribute anything to the local chantry. And both Nicolai and DuSable seemed to disobey the Pyramid on occasion. They don't get hunted down and destroyed for disobeying. They just don't get to rise within the clan hierarchy or benefit from that social solidarity. It's more about peer pressure, not getting supported later should you need it, and the fear whether you'll be mentioned in the will. Now that doesn't mean you can't have some local chantry of board or salon or whatever hunt down and destroy a vampire of that clan for somehow not towing the line. But that's because the head vampire is some kind of psychopath or tyrant. It's not part of the clan. Only if someone is seen to have truly betrayed the entire family might something like that happen.<br /> <br /> The other thing about clans is that they become more important the older the vampire gets. A neonate still has many ties to the mortal world. They have friends and family members from the time they were still living. They have interests and passions from their mortal dies that still motivate them. The world around them is what they know and understand. However, as time passages, their ties to the mortal world passes. Not only their old friends and families, but even things we often think as more permanent like social institutions, countries, religion, and more can either end or change into an unrecognizable form sharing only the name. But the clan remains the same. The elders continue to live, and their culture survives. As influence among mortals are seen to fade and end, power and influence within the clan gains greater importance and seen as something more permanent. So clans are much more important to the elders than to neonates.<br /> <br /> As for the individual clans themselves, almost anything important about them can be found in the typical two page clan write ups in the corebooks, plus the few pages given in the Players Guide. The clanbooks typically provide more details, but aren't actually needed. The unique information there is more like trivia to namedrop, than something that should cause you to run things differently from the basics provided in the corebook and Players Guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T04:55:04-07:00","id":1466443,"title":"","content":"<b>How do I roleplay the Clans 4#: Malkavians</b><br /> <br /> As a general rule, I think Malkavians are people who should have understated insanity. It's not that it's not there but I think a good more than half of Malkavians are perfectly high-functioning and able to fit into Kindred society just fine.<br /> <br /> I think I used the description, &quot;The majority of Malkavian derangements are narcissism, megalomania, blood obsession, reduced empathy [roll Humanity for 2 stains instead of one], berserk fury, paranoia, and sanguinary animism [Your Beast talks to you].&quot; In short, the vast majority of Malkavians are people who have only slightly exaggerated or perhaps even precocious versions of what Elder vampires already have out of habit.<br /> <br /> I tend to suggest Malkavians tend to have lower Humanity than the majority of Kindred in the Camarilla but they tend to stabilize a lot faster. So the majority of Malkavians you'll meet are around 5-6 Humanity as Fledglings and Neonates. They are removed from Humanity in the same way the Tzimisce tend to be, though on a different path. One player of mine came up with a very interesting idea to separate the Malkavian derangement from &quot;mortal&quot; derangements as well by taking some elements from the Daughters of Cacophany. All Malkavians are hearing SOMETHING all the time in the background of their minds. Words of Malkav or other Malkavians perhaps but develop their frailties as a means of trying to cope with the<br /> concept.<br /> <br /> I do think that the &quot;Trickster&quot; archetype is alive and well among Malkavians with the fact they are people who very often have questionable desire for power and prestige compared to other Kindred. As such, they are often people who enjoy bringing down the haughty and prideful for no other reason than they can. These aren't the majority of Malkavians but it's a tradition in their clan and they have a decent chunk among the Anarchs unlike what V5 says.<br /> <br /> The use of Auspex, Dominate, and Obfuscate also means that Malkavians are able to gain insights into what other Kindred are up to better than people think. Unlike the Nosferatu, they aren't generally information brokers but still gather secrets as a way of forwarding their own plans or sabotaging the plans of others. Generally, other Kindred underestimate what Malkavian spies are up to because they either believe that the Kindred are receiving &quot;signals&quot; from their abilities or because they don't think Malkavians are capable of the long-term planning that other Kindred are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:22:50-07:00","id":1466562,"title":"","content":"<b>Toreador</b><br /> <br /> <i>Embrace:</i> More than most other clans, especially with so much prestige, the Toreador are likely to be extremely personal on their Embraces. But it isn't that the Clan won't judge it, quite the contrary. They'll <i>definitely</i> judge a member's choice and procedure. Still, that only means localized social pressure, instead of any organized standard.<br /> <br /> This makes the Toreador an extremely diversified clan. That may be one of the things that keep them at least decent at socializing, as they have to adjust to what is actually a pretty diverse family. It also means Childe are quite affected by their interpersonal relationship with their Sire, as other clan members and greater clan culture intrudes little. After that they're shaped by their interactions with the local Kindred society, including clan members.<br /> <br /> <i>Structure:</i> the clan has little in terms of structure, instead focusing on just keeping in touch and sharing interests. Their strength and their weakness as Kindred is their ability to exist in society, so they must have theirs in some form.<br /> <br /> This makes them used to deal with diversity and dynamic interactions, more than actually forces them into any form of conformity. Except, of course, that it also exposes everyone among them to their best bullies. In such a situation no Toreador can be indifferent to the opinions of their peers for long, and most sharpen their senses to deal with it.<br /> <br /> Some may actually retract and try to not get a lot of attention. They may be numerous, but by virtue of their behavior they also don't weigh much in the clan's reputation, so their actual numbers don't matter.<br /> <br /> <i>Weakness:</i> beauty is in the eye of the beholder, but it doesn't change that the clan weakness makes every Toreador keenly aware of how it affects people. After all, they may be more susceptible, but no one is actually immune.<br /> <br /> It also creates a survival pressure few Kindred comprehend. Toreador go to great lengths to fill their havens and lives with beauty because they will <i>die</i> if they don't. Why? Simply put, if they don't inure themselves by excessive contact with beauty, the very world around them becomes a life-threatening danger.<br /> <br /> Have you ever had a moment when you found out of a sudden that a little thing you usually take for granted is actually very beautiful? Or found a beautiful image, art piece or person, when you simply weren't expecting? A Toreador isn't actually more likely or interested in such things, but they can become <i>entranced </i>by such fleeting moments all the same regardless of how much they really want to pay attention.<br /> <br /> So it is better to be surrounded by beauty and raise your standards as much as possible, so you're not likely to freeze in place when you definitely shouldn't. And if the other clans think low of you, fuck them, they don't give you blood, keep your roof or pay your bills, do they?<br /> <br /> <i>Disciplines:</i> Presence makes you the most beautiful thing around. With all you learn from your weakness, it's logical to learn to use this aspect of the Discipline. Even because you know very well that it only goes so far into shaping emotions, the other half is always in the beholder's eye again, so you're kind of stuck with it, like it or not. You know beauty, live surrounded by beauty, and other Kindred probably only see you as that. It's not as if any of them will remember you by your effect on mortals...<br /> <br /> Auspex is almost as much a curse as a blessing at first, as the Toreador have to bear an even more colorful and detailed perception of reality. But it also helps in seeing hidden ugliness as much as beauty. As it grows in power the Kindred acquires an excellent window in the emotions of others that goes well by itself or in tandem with Presence.<br /> <br /> Celerity is extremely versatile ass it helps you to be where you want when you want, be it at Elysium or out of Dodge. Of course, its uses in combat also mean a Toreador can be a capable duelist (great for dramatic flair in court) or a very capable fighter when they decide the other stuff isn't really their thing. A diverse physical Discipline for a diverse clan.<br /> <br /> <i>Culture:</i> Toreador culture is more informed by their shared experiences in Kindred society than by shared goals, dogma or what have you. Beauty is always in their talks as much because they learn to appreciate it as a way for them to share survival strategies.<br /> <br /> Outside that, though, it isn't a club, a cult or an enterprise. It is a society. They have little in common except their need of socializing for the sake of self preservation and no pressure to isolate. And while it isn't a safe place in most reasonable standards, it is still a place where being emotional and vulnerable is too common to be a problem.<br /> <br /> <i>Characters:</i> A Toreador can be almost anyone and anything, with a twist of being outwardly an hedonist, or just not be seen at all as a member of the clan.<br /> <br /> Seeking beauty in safe circumstances becomes quickly second nature after the first time that you lose hours of your night out of a sudden stuck in place. This is a very scary situation, the sensation of loosing yourself.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, socialization informs a lot of those characters in very different ways. Many learn to derive power from it, many just feel better within any social gathering. Sometimes it is just their yearning for company, but at other times it is the safety of having someone nearby that can get you out of a reverie.<br /> <br /> Those who avoid large gatherings may still seek groups they feel safe with, and they quickly become the social glue of those. Others may avoid socialization entirely, as their reputation is actually far out of proportion.<br /> <br /> What they can't avoid, though, is the impression they leave in the other Kindred and the feedback loop it creates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T20:46:43-07:00","id":1466600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465949-world-building-how-do-you-use-certain-clans?p=1466443#post1466443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How do I roleplay the Clans 4#: Malkavians</b><br /> <br /> As a general rule, I think Malkavians are people who should have understated insanity. It's not that it's not there but I think a good more than half of Malkavians are perfectly high-functioning and able to fit into Kindred society just fine.<br /> <br /> I think I used the description, &quot;The majority of Malkavian derangements are narcissism, megalomania, blood obsession, reduced empathy [roll Humanity for 2 stains instead of one], berserk fury, paranoia, and sanguinary animism [Your Beast talks to you].&quot; In short, the vast majority of Malkavians are people who have only slightly exaggerated or perhaps even precocious versions of what Elder vampires already have out of habit.<br /> <br /> I tend to suggest Malkavians tend to have lower Humanity than the majority of Kindred in the Camarilla but they tend to stabilize a lot faster. So the majority of Malkavians you'll meet are around 5-6 Humanity as Fledglings and Neonates. They are removed from Humanity in the same way the Tzimisce tend to be, though on a different path. One player of mine came up with a very interesting idea to separate the Malkavian derangement from &quot;mortal&quot; derangements as well by taking some elements from the Daughters of Cacophany. All Malkavians are hearing SOMETHING all the time in the background of their minds. Words of Malkav or other Malkavians perhaps but develop their frailties as a means of trying to cope with the<br /> concept.<br /> <br /> I do think that the &quot;Trickster&quot; archetype is alive and well among Malkavians with the fact they are people who very often have questionable desire for power and prestige compared to other Kindred. As such, they are often people who enjoy bringing down the haughty and prideful for no other reason than they can. These aren't the majority of Malkavians but it's a tradition in their clan and they have a decent chunk among the Anarchs unlike what V5 says.<br /> <br /> The use of Auspex, Dominate, and Obfuscate also means that Malkavians are able to gain insights into what other Kindred are up to better than people think. Unlike the Nosferatu, they aren't generally information brokers but still gather secrets as a way of forwarding their own plans or sabotaging the plans of others. Generally, other Kindred underestimate what Malkavian spies are up to because they either believe that the Kindred are receiving &quot;signals&quot; from their abilities or because they don't think Malkavians are capable of the long-term planning that other Kindred are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've been distancing myself from the classic Malkavian tropes, but I think they can be awesome characters of many depths. I see them as having the worst bouts of compulsion or passion (more the classical bad type of passion), not being crazy, but having one or more specific conditions, that might be only mental, or might be physical too. V5 helped me turn this more true, for it doesn't need to be a single defined or human condition, it might be a nerve wracking flashback or paranoia, a great depression, a tiring weight upon the shoulders and eyes, a terrible obsession coming bare, or simply the suppression of any shame, care, etiquette or social contract. <br /> <br /> Each Malk will respond differently to their bane, some might embrace it, others might mentally suppress it, act like it doesn't exist with sincere ignorance, others might hate, fear or have shame of it. All in all I think they mostly are the Clan with the most self-controlled members, for they have some of the most self-destructive inflictions. As such, they learn to control themselves, and to understand themselves to better hold back, or even to weaponize their infliction (Dementation is a more literal and powerful approach to this yeah). <br /> <br /> Also, to me, the Malkavians function highly as the vampires who stare at the &lt;Abyss, Blood, Cosmos, whatever&gt; so that other vampires don't have too. What is shattered may not be broken, or if it is, it's harder to break. So they don't ignore problems, they are the first to point them out (be it for insightful wits, or real auspicious and prophetic sight); although they are also Cursed with that which afflicted Cassandra from Troy, very few times they are heard, and so their wise council fall in deaf ears.<br /> <br /> Malkavian politicians and power brokers must be one of the toughest nuts to crack. To read them is hard, to find them and catch them off guard is harder (their Disciplines are the thick icing on the cake). Thing is, once you get to use their affliction against them, they've already lost. Many times, they truly are vampires that &quot;live on the moon&quot;, but that also means they decide or know when the tides are rising, and when they are lowering. <br /> <br /> One thing I'm constantly thinking is the that Trickster or Jester side of things. Sometimes it feels like a diversion from the deep and dirty secrets the Malkavians trully work with. Other times I imagine they would feel ashamed or even bothered by the image that the most trickster-jesters Malks make for the Clan (which in some ways it could be a fishmalk member); and they would themselves hunt the most deranged members, like knights that hunter wights. <br /> <br /> But yeah, I really like the Malkavians, and they have lot of untapped potential, but sadly they are mostly portrayed as the quirky, weird and nuts character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T07:02:17-07:00","id":1466644,"title":"","content":"<b>Tremere</b><br /> <br /> <i>Embrace:</i> more than Ventrue, the Tremere are a tightly controlled structure. Way before you earn the right for Embrace from your Prince you must earn it from your clan. It is a proposal for an initiation. Your chantry and its peers will discuss the candidates, evaluate, compare.<br /> <br /> Which Embrace has something to add to the Warlocks? Even an approval is less about you being rewarded with the right of siring, and more about being recognized as the one who brought the most promising apprentice. They are not your childe more than a new member of the clan.<br /> <br /> This selection process is long, structured and pragmatic. Observe and take notes about candidates. Write a thorough report about their strengths, their benefits to the clan, weaknesses, verifiable knowledge, ending with a pitch on why they should be brought in. Add to it regularly, with new observations and test results on the candidate.<br /> <br /> Candidates may be chosen for any reason. The ability to learn and develop the arcane arts of the clan is highly desirable, but not always required. They may have valuable knowledge in areas the clan still needs, talent acquiring material resources, sometimes a new perspective that can provide insight in the development of new Paths of Blood Magic, or just be well positioned in a number of ways. But the clan will hardly suffer stupidity or incompetence if a candidate can't hugely compensate this in some way.<br /> <br /> <i>Structure:</i> the Tremere can barely be called a clan in the more familial sense of the word. Anyone that can't fit in the hierarchy isn't just a pariah, but a full liability to be brought down. They are an occult order and an army. You have a position in the hierarchy, benefits and functions, a superior to answer to, a number of responsibilities.<br /> <br /> Obedience isn't an option. You don't belong to your Sire or to a culture. Your personal beliefs are irrelevant as long as you comprehend loyalty isn't in any way a choice. You're watched and evaluated, and non compliance or lack of value isn't just grounds to removal of benefits, but to outright termination of your &quot;employment&quot; and benefits, including the benefit of living.<br /> <br /> Being a Tremere isn't only enslavement, of course. With the same amount of exigence come the benefits. What the clan require, the clan provide the means to achieve. Even a small chantry is also library, university campus, fortress, communication point and shelter. Most likely an armory. Your superiors are demanding, but they are also very clear in their demands, as Tremere have no use for wordplay and pretense among themselves.<br /> <br /> And finally, as long as you meet basic expectations and don't put it at risk, the clan won't care about your personal affairs. Culture and belief are not of their concern. You may benefit greatly from your efforts to grow in the Pyramid if you have the ambition for it, but you're also left to your devices if you just want to fulfill your quota and go home.<br /> <br /> More than many other clans the Tremere knows what it means to <b>be </b>more of an organization than infiltrating them. And as such, they know ambition plays a huge role in their midst and must be rewarded, but so does simple conformity. Ambition will be rewarded, though, and they have many ways to do so, from bits of knowledge or special work or learning opportunities, to an endless ladder of positions in their occult hierarchy when a member prove themselves and outsmart their rivals.<br /> <br /> <i>Weakness:</i> in a sense, there is none. The Tremere were self-Embraced and no such a thing exists among them as understood by other Kindred. They're as perfect as a powerful Caitiff can be. The Pyramid certainly has no weakness.<br /> <br /> For individual Tremere their weakness is the clan. Whatever version of their weakness you use, they individually pay for the practices of the clan to control them. The leaders of this big scheme don't trust their underlings in any meaningful way and use their magics freely on them.<br /> <br /> Your blood is in their possession. Literally. At least a few drops are safely guarded at secret locations where some of your superiors may access it to work their sympathetic magics on you. If you're weak against Blood Bonds it is because they made you so to have you pliable. If instead you are incapable of Bonding, it is because they took it from you so you can't ever use this against them. If they didn't did anything like that, then they at least started Bonding you already. And if they didn't case your weakness on purpose, it's still a side effect of their magics on you.<br /> <br /> My personal preferred version is that the clan became incapable of Blood Bond recently, as some in the Council of Seven finally achieved to enact a ritual to this effect. They had been victims to it for about a thousand years, and have no love for this ability. The Bond clouds the mind with unhealthy emotion, is unnecessary when they have your blood and their magics and above all else, this ritual freed them finally from Tremere, the Founder.<br /> <br /> <i>Disciplines:</i> it is hard to say when their signature Disciplines came to be that. Was it by design, accident or through effort? Only very few among them can surely know the answer, but it is nonetheless as set that serves well their organization.<br /> <br /> The Tremere's approach to Discipline use is open and direct. They're not a manifestation of personality or anything, just straightforward tools. You are a student and researcher, and so expected to gather information. You will not suffer resistance to the clan's orders, Dominate ensure obedience. Thaumaturgy is the Great Work and Tool of the clan, questioning it isn't a point.<br /> <br /> What's more interesting than their spread is the unique relation they have with their powers. They covet their secrets, but freely offer their services. Clan members are encouraged to exhibit some powers freely so everyone knows what they can offer. They're maybe the most unashamed users of Dominate, and they don't pretend to not make free use of their Auspex.<br /> <br /> Not that they're careless about this, they pretty much have to be. Instead, while other Kindred use their Disciplines to grab influence and power, the Tremere as a clan use theirs as bargaining chips and arguments.<br /> <br /> Of course, they have secret plans, but that's the gist of their relationship with their supernatural powers. And how you use yours on your personal life won't change how you're required to do your actual job for the clan.<br /> <br /> <i>Culture:</i> as an academic and militaristic organization, the Tremere have a strong internal culture with not as much pressure for a member to belong. For those who dive in, it is a world in itself that greatly rewards ambition and intellect, and impressing your superiors is of utmost importance, while surpassing your peers is an absolute necessity through either hard work or sabotage.<br /> <br /> For those who abstain from it, is at the same time a source of security and oppression. You have obligations to fulfill and superiors measuring your performance, but you also have this same structure to give you stability. Luck have a role to play, as you may be positioned in a key station where your challenges are big and constant, or may have just a few obligations beyond weekly reports and annual tests.<br /> <br /> You are never invisible to the system, though, and that guarantees every member develop some sort of paranoia.<br /> <br /> <i>Characters:</i> as members from a driven organization with a global strategy and structured work, the Tremere are varied but enslaved to a will above their own.<br /> <br /> It is less that they have a lot in common and more that they have to play the part. Some relish it. Some resent it profoundly. Some are good at it and others don't, the clan doesn't always require that you pretend to like it in front of others.<br /> <br /> Many learn to act in the shadows, where the clan can't see them (or at least they think it can't). Some do so to rebel, although not always in a big way. Many just want to sabotage internal rivals. Others want to &quot;breath&quot; a little, only. Even the most loyal learn to hide failure and problems that the upper echelons may worry about out of proportion. The clan, of course, is completely aware of this fact.<br /> <br /> But in the open the Tremere make sure that your individuality simply don't matter. You are a servant of the Pyramid and act as its eyes and hands. Anyone who thinks otherwise is a fool and they know it as well as you do, regardless of what you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T09:09:50-07:00","id":1466775,"title":"","content":"<b>Malkavian</b><br /> <br /> ===============<br /> <br /> <u><i>On the matter of Madness:</i></u> It is easy to play madness for laughs. It is also easy to condemn the practice. What isn't so easy is to decide what to do with it and how it should be played.<br /> <br /> Some may avoid &quot;overt&quot; derangement altogether, thinking they're silly by nature. I don't think many of the actual people that suffer from them would agree. But then, it may be just a matter of comfort zone. That's ok, but limiting. In the end I can give some advice, but it's hard to define and decide.<br /> <br /> My favorite NPC Malkavian is the Voerman &quot;Sisters&quot;. A very overt form of madness not being played for laughs or for gore. Both personalities are competent and interesting characters in their own right, and their changes in control aren't random, either.<br /> <br /> The advice I can give is this: if you want to portray a person with mental health issues, ask an actual person with similar issues. <b>We</b> are not in the dark anymore in those days. Many of us have normal lives despite our neurological and/or psychological differences, and many became bloggers, vloggers, etc, talking about our conditions on the internet. You will find out how it really is like to live with things like Schizophrenia and Dissociative Disorders.<br /> <br /> Also learn a little about some definitions on disorders, but a quick primer on it, though:<br /> <br /> <b><i>Madness</i></b> - is primarily a social perception. Although many people think that it equates to &quot;mental disease&quot;, this isn't actually true;<br /> <br /> <b><i>Insanity</i></b> - is actually a legal term. Isn't about how much a person needs health care or anything, but just about how much the person can be deemed guilty of a crime. Voerman isn't insane, not even when she killed her father (although she was a child, so not guilty by default);<br /> <br /> <b><i>Disorder</i></b> - is the actual medical term, and comes in many forms and variations. It is based on adaptability, though, so many weird behaviors that would be promptly regarded as madness aren't disorders, and the opposite is also true. I have <i>Autism Spectrum Disorder</i>;<br /> <br /> <b><i>Randomness</i></b> - is a common misconception about mental health problems. People seem as Mad are frequently regarded as incomprehensible and random by observers, but this is mostly born out of a disconnection in perception. As a rule of thumb, <i>Disorders</i> are far more marked by a difficulty in breaking patterns than in following them, even if not the patterns that people expect.<br /> <br /> ============<br /> <br /> <i>Embrace:</i> no clan-wide rule or expectation exists about embraces in the clan. The few things it expects in a new member will be brought up by the process anyway.<br /> <br /> Many Embrace while at the mercy of their Weakness in some way. And many <i>pretend</i> to have done so. In fact, Malkavians aren't the only clan without any rules for Embraces, but they're the most likely to <i>ignore the Domain rules and get away with it</i>. It's so the <i>de facto</i> most diverse clan around by far.<br /> <br /> <i>Structure:</i> one change in Revised isn't an actual change, as it was there in their description since always, the <i>Malkavian Madness Network</i>. The clan have a loose structure where very few demands are thrown on its members, but they have more contact than any other clan.<br /> <br /> The nature of this structure is mostly social, with a heavy exchange of news and support. Malkavians know each other and exchange news on their side of the world, some may have an alliance and share particular pieces of information, and everyone is welcome to just hang around at a safe place.<br /> <br /> If there's one rule it's this: the Network is a safe place. Everyone have issues, everyone needs a place where they can speak out their thing without being judged. If the clan can't provide, they'll be overwhelmed by other's prejudice and collectively weaken. You don't have to like your clan mates, but respect them in the Network.<br /> <br /> What makes this structure special and baffles the other clans is the fact that Malkavians interact in their own minds, either because their Ante became a hive-mind of sorts, or just because some members use their own Auspex to set up their meetings.<br /> <br /> <i>Weakness:</i> the seeds of madness lie in the minds of everyone, and the Malkavian Curse makes it bloom in its most absolute glory. That is an unsettling experience as your own mind craft your customized condition just by growing something out of proportion.<br /> <br /> Out of the deal comes overblown prejudice and new understanding of the human mind, especially your own.<br /> <br /> In the end, though, the prejudice part is what makes this weakness be a social glue for the clan. The inner experiences are too unique, as are the individual reactions to them. But the outside experiences of how the others react to the mere mention of your clan's name, that's the way the other clans show to you where your home is.<br /> <br /> <i>Disciplines:</i> it's complicated to separate the Clan Disciplines from the Clan Weakness with the Malkavian. Auspex gives access to information outside the perceptions of other Kindred, Obfuscate make other look the other way or let you be whomever you want to be, Dominate and Dementation mess with the minds and emotions of others.<br /> <br /> But being mad makes a bad night do pretty much the same things, in a way. At least that's what most people think, and isn't completely untrue.<br /> <br /> What can then be said for sure is that those powers work even more to set the Kindred apart from its &quot;normal&quot; peers, every use of them being either an alienating experience or the forceful imposition of yourself on others. It's also a great way to delve deeper on one's own problems.<br /> <br /> That belies, though, one of the most powerful Discipline spreads when used together. Combined those three Disciplines strengthen each other to astounding degrees, as they cover each other limitations.<br /> <br /> <i>Culture:</i> with a common experience of alienation and contact through the Madness Network, Malkavians tend to have a strong sense of community and a somewhat supportive attitude towards one another.<br /> <br /> They meet in mind or body, they talk about their stuff, share information, find others with similar experience or at least find people that won't look them with fear or pity in the eyes. This tends to be an important fixture in their lives, so as much as they're not of a single purpose, few among them won't fight to keep things that way.<br /> <br /> Keeping the workings of this community from being understood by other vampires is also a common cause, as any Malkavian that could care to make it clearer also understands the advantage of not doing so. Only a Malkavian can truly participate directly and without risking their own mind, so they're not only an excellent way to keep people guessing and nervous, they're also excellent to discuss important stuff protected from prying eyes.<br /> <br /> <i>Characters:</i> Anyone can become a Malkavian. But no one can make it unscathed.<br /> <br /> Building a Malk demands a deeper than normal examination of the character's psyche. Legend says that only people with already a foot in madness is chosen for the Embrace, but truth is that &quot;madness&quot; is just a little twist in normal human experience. You can't be human and not have a foot there.<br /> <br /> So the process comes down to examine the character and find the seed you'll use to build their unique mind, then choose the way it will go from &quot;normal&quot; to &quot;mad&quot;. Then, as you revisit the character's story through the lens of the new madness, it becomes easy to reinterpret their lives as unhinged from start.<br /> <br /> What else informs a Malkavian distinctly from a random character is the &quot;Malkavian treatment&quot;. How people around you deal with your condition? How did other Kindred reacted when learning your clan? How did you dealt with the Network? The experiences brought by the mere fact of being a Malkavian may bring succor, resentment, sometimes even be more traumatic than any cause for their specific madness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T10:22:33-07:00","id":1466959,"title":"","content":"One of the best pieces of advice I've ever heard on playing Malkavians - it may have been from one of the Clanbooks - is to actually play your character's Nature and Demeanor instead of forgetting them. Let the Demeanor be the character when they're composed, and the Nature be the character during their episodes. Mechanical incentives are already in place, in the form of Willpower restoration. The Clan Madness comes and goes as the player seeks the Willpower reward in response to circumstances around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}